WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.460
And you can sit there.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.200
Then we can start!

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.600
Ada Hegerberg ...

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.280
I'm not sure whether you or I should say welcome, because we're sitting in Lyon -

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.940
- at a quite chilly football field.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.320
But I'll say welcome anyways!

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.720
Okay. Merci!

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:18.880
Bienvenue!

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.060
How French have you become?

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:27.240
A Norwegian soul with a little touch of frenchness, I would say.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.120
Four and a half years, it's been quite some time, now.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.880
Do you speak French?

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.020
Yes, I do.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.140
Well?

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:40.420
That was my first ambition when I came here, the French, I needed to learn that straight away.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.740
You're the only woman in the world who has the Ballon d'Or.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.400
... Which is the golden ball, which you won on December 3rd.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.240
If you close your eyes and think of that night ...

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.680
What's your strongest memory?

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.100
I would say the mutual respect that was there throughout the evening.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.780
It was such a powerful feeling to be present in -

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.040
- such a big group of big profiles, I would say.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.740
And to feel that much at home.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:12.120
And to feel that everyone respects each other for the work that is being done.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.480
And to simply just celebrate -

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.700
- football at its highest level. And that -

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.960
That was very motivating, and a huge thing to see. For the future as well.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:25.340
It was definitely about you -

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.720
- but you also became a symbol of something.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.960
Yes. The night was about so much more than me.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.340
I really felt that throughout the whole day, and also after.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.940
It was a historical moment, and -

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.140
I feel that -

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.580
- everyone took part in it.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:47.160
All girls, all women, both those who play football and those who don't.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:53.700
To be the centre of a night like that was one of the biggest experiences of my life.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.260
And it was bigger than me, because -

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.940
It was a big step in the right direction, for a lot of girls.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.660
To set yourself a goal -

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.640
- to become the world's best player -

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.500
- when in the process did you do that?

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.740
The goal-oriented person in me appeared little after little when I was around 10-11-12.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.960
It was a little later than my siblings.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.160
They were big stars in the family.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.580
Because you're definitely from a football family?

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.680
Yes. Mom and dad have played, my brother has played, Andrine plays in Paris Saint-Germain.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.100
I didn't really have a choice. I would return from handball training and skiin and everything, but football was -

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.500
- the deal.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:40.500
But it takes a lot of self discipline.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:49.040
And ... I like to say that you need to dream big, but you also need to know the consequences of dreaming big.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.380
Yes, because this didn't happen without pain?

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.940
And you're very well known for your self discipline, you're known for -

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.500
- your ability to train a lot.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:07.800
Can you describe for us what your training has been like at its most demanding?

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:14.120
That happened quite often when we were around 13-14, that our dad pushed us quite hard, to know -

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.460
- where we were when we were at the bottom.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.860
And that was such a hard mental training that from there, it only went up.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.960
And that taught us how we could train.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.420
And it gave us self confidence.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.340
Because we knew that we were well trained.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.360
And then we could just go for it.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.780
But if you imagine that now, there's -

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:39.540
- lots of sports parents watching you -

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.340
- and, of course, a lot of young, potentially good, football players.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.720
How hard should they be pushed, and how much should they want it themselves?

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.340
I've always gotten the question: «Is this what you want?».

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.520
And I've of course answered: «Yes. This is what I want».

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.380
And then you're there 100 percent.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:04.140
But if I've said that «this is enough for me», then they've stepped down and let it be.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.700
So they haven't dragged you out in the rain to ..?

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:07.660
No, no, no!

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:13.780
The wish to do it needs to lay with the individual, or me, or children, or youth.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:17.660
The desire to be good needs to come from deep inside, and you need to -

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.780
- know that you need to do all the hard work.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.300
But you need someone to help you push.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:25.100
And I needed someone to push. And I wanted them on my team, and then it was -

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.000
- a huge support. But they also pushed me.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.020
When you won the Ballon d'Or in December -

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.620
- that was -

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.440
- in a way a turning point that said something about -

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.200
- how we now see a different future for women's football.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.280
But someone who represented the past that day was a French DJ -

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.520
- who managed to ask if you could twerk.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.800
Which is a dance where you shake your bottom.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.600
When you received the award.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.540
Which was a strange thing to ask, and something he received a lot of criticism for.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.720
Did he ever apologise to you?

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.640
He said he was sorry after the fuss started.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:10.040
Because there was a lot of fuss, but I didn't realise that until later, because I didn't have time to  -

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.800
- to look at anything. And it exploded on social media and -

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:20.240
And I just thought it was a strange question. It would have been just as strange if a man had been asked the same question.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.560
That's what I thought.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.020
So he came over and apologised, and I said «the show must go on».

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.900
And I didn't put any more energy into it.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.500
So that was a very unfortunate turn.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.880
For his part. But people are on the alert.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.300
People are on the alert with regards to these kinds of -

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.780
- comments. And that might show even more -

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.780
- that we've come a little further.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.680
At the same time, I think that there are many other problems -

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.420
- that are worse than this case -

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.260
- that should be elevated.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:01.200
So that night it just ended in a lot of laughs, at the whole thing.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:02.980
Because you ...

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.680
He can play for free at my wedding!

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.220
That's the least he can do!

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:14.620
Do you now live like this football millionaire?

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.580
I treat myself to a duck breast now and then!

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.540
A duck breast?!

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:18.300
Yes!

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:22.320
My boyfriend and I cook duck breasts sometimes.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.520
We have a good life, absolutely.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:25.900
But ...

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:30.600
But I'm a regular person from Sunndal who has a normal life in Lyon, I would say.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:31.500
Yes.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.660
But there are a lot of football players with success abroad who have -

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.480
- shown that they have that success!

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.540
I don't have a Ferrari or a Porsche or anything like that.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.980
You haven't bought yourself an expensive care because you ..?

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:44.740
No. But it's quite funny, because -

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.400
Right after I received the Golden Ball -

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.380
I left my car at the repair shop, because someone had put a dent in it.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.540
And ...

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:56.580
I got a really nice Tuscon as a replacement car, a four wheel drive -

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.740
- and it was extremely nice, with heated seats and -

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.760
And I drove that -

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:07.480
- to the training facility the day after Ballon d'Or.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.240
And I thought, «oh no, oh no, oh no».

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.700
«Don't let anyone see me in this car, the day after this!»

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.260
So I just hurried out of the car and into the football club.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.760
And I got there and thought «phew». But everyone had seen it.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:22.120
«Ah, so you just went completely overboard after that event!»

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.020
So they thought you had bought this huge car just the day after!

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.060
So now I've gotten my old car back.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.440
My dad called me the other day and ...

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.300
«Have you gotten your old car back?». And I said «no, I haven't yet».

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:37.460
And he said: «I think you should get it back soon». And I said: «Dad, let me live like this for just a moment!»

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:38.900
But my old car is back.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.780
We also have to talk about the Norwegian national team.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:49.320
And there, you've sort of become the black sheep.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:54.660
And I have to say that because you're actually sitting in a black sheep «fur»!

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.700
Nice word play!

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:02.360
But what happened there?

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.400
You left the team after -

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.680
The European Championship in 2017, which was a bad championship for Norway.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.080
And you had a break.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:17.520
And that break has turned into a more permanent ending.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.600
The thing is that I've never felt that I've been able to influence in the way I would've liked to influence.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:28.080
And I've heard a lot of things and there's been fuss about that I wanted to control the team and who plays -

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.660
- but we've never talked about it like that.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:37.480
I quite frankly just felt that I've contributed with what I could contribute with, but it hasn't been enough.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:40.460
And when I can't be a part of it myself anymore ...

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:45.380
... and contribute with what I know, and then be placed in a system that ...

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.340
... doesn't fit me, simply.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.580
Then I can't continue.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.740
In a way that they tried to curb you, or ..?

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:52.900
Yes, quite simply.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:55.600
I've always had a lot of ambition.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.940
And I've always had a lot of ambition on behalf of the team.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.080
That we should be able to well together.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.880
And that ...

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:09.000
That hasn't worked. And there was a lot of fuss. And that fuss ...

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.460
I really could do without.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.800
Because I'm the one left with the consequences of quitting, not having a national team to play for.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:18.020
I was very open to an open dialogue.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:21.340
And I'm very honest, about everything ...

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.060
... internally.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.900
I don't have a need to discuss anything in the media.

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:29.460
But there was a huge fuss. So ...

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.800
My goal was to keep focusing.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.340
To move the focus to the next day, the next thing.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.600
And that has been the goal ever since, and that has worked very well.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.400
And ...

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.840
That's the way I'm going to keep doing it.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.320
What needs to change for you to return?

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.860
Is there a long list of points?

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.020
There are clear points.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.280
That's a thing that's between them and me.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.920
And I don't have a need to share that with the rest.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.980
And I think that ...

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:02.940
It's up to them, really.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:06.600
I made my decision and am content with that.

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:11.580
I'm very confident that I made the right decision to move on in my career. And ...

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:17.140
But we Norwegians, we have the world's best football player, but at the same time, we don't ..!

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:23.120
Yes! And that's absurd! Because I've never felt as Norwegian as I do now!

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:28.040
And a Norwegian who wins a Ballon d'Or, to me, that's incredible!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.120
And I'm so proud of that.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:38.200
To come from a small place in Sunndal in Møre og Romsdal and stand on stage in front of the entire football world and receive a golden ball -

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:41.440
- is so extremely inspiring to me.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:46.120
And it shows that no matter where you're from, if you think outside the box and work hard, then -

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.640
You can make it!

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:53.360
So even though I don't play for a national team, I'm -

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.140
- extremely sad that I can't play for my country.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:01.200
But in this particular case, I had to make a decision to be able to move on.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.140
And I ...

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:09.320
... am not losing my nationality because of that. I hope people don't forget that.

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:10.560
You still have your passport?

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.540
I bring my passport everywhere, it's safe in my living room!

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.140
What's your plan?

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.160
You have the Ballon d'Or, there isn't very much more ...

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:24.360
... to get?

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:25.780
Yes, there is!

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:26.720
Can you get better?

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:27.780
Yes.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.280
A lot better, I think.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:31.480
I'm very optimistic about that.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:32.980
I hope.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:38.480
But Ada, thank you so much for being part of this, and for letting us come to Lyon to meet you!

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.920
It's big for me as well. Thank you so much!

